    "text_delta": "th.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a polite, professional follow-up:**\n   Reach out to the HR contact or hiring lead. Frame your request around personal and professional development rather than challenging the decision:\n   > *\"Thank you again for the opportunity to interview for the Head of Structural Engineering role. I know the team is busy, but as I reflect on my career and prepare for future leadership opportunities, any specific feedback on how I can strengthen my profile—or areas where the successful candidate stood out—would be immensely valuable.\"*\n\n2. **Focus on commercial and leadership feedback:**\n   When you do speak with them or receive feedback, ask targeted questions:\n   * How was your vision for the group received?\n   * Were there gaps identified in business development, commercial strategy, or client engagement?\n   * How did they view your interview presentation relative to their strategic goals?\n\n3. **Protect your professional capital:**\n   Senior engineering circles are small, and consulting firms frequently reconsider strong runners-up for future leadership, director-level, or principal specialist roles. Approaching the outcome with professionalism and curiosity keeps that door open.\n",
